\subsection{Channel A: similarity-weighted aggregation}
Weighting neighbors by embedding similarity removed most of that loss, because a site at the border of an anomaly is averaged mainly with anomalous neighbors (Table~\ref{tab:ap}, Fig.~\ref{fig:rules}). The untuned $3\times3$ rule reached $F=$ @F_SIMW@, @D_SIMW_MEAN@ above the fixed mean and @D_SIMW_NONE@ above no smoothing (paired 95\% intervals). In the controlled generator the fixed mean did not beat no smoothing in any of the @CS_N@ cohorts, while similarity weighting beat both in all @CS_N@ (mean AP @LF_APN@, @LF_APM@ and @LF_APS@). It kept the region recall of scattered anomalies at @R_SIMW_SC@ and of bars at @R_SIMW_BAR@, lowered the false regions per image from @FR_NONE@ to @FR_SIMW@, and raised the DINOv2 image AP to @T_SIMW_D@. It did not help the handcrafted-feature images (@T_SIMW_H@, against @T_NONE_H@ without smoothing), and on the rotor-only lattices it stayed slightly below no smoothing (@T_SIMW_ROT@ against @T_NONE_ROT@). The range of the average precision over the six anomaly shapes was @RG_NONE@ without smoothing, @RG_MEAN@ for the fixed mean and @RG_SIMW@ for similarity weighting.

